WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.136
- What if we have
15 or 20% inflation

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.138
by November or December?

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:08.341 align:start position:0%
We're talking about an alarming
problem where, you know,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:09.976
the poor and working
class in our country

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.912
won't be able to afford the
routine staples of life.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:14.381
But we're then talking also

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:17.250 align:start size:88% position:13%
about what happens
when it finally bursts.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when it bursts usually
you have dramatic rises

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.855
in interest rates,

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.557 align:start size:97% position:3%
but you also have dramatically
high unemployment.

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:27.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm concerned about
the future of our country.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.129
And I think we need to
get our house in order.

00:00:29.129 --> 00:00:31.731
(upbeat music)

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:38.671 line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin and joining
me today is one of the senators

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:40.840 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
from the great
state of Kentucky.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.943 line:0%
Senator Rand Paul, welcome
back to the Rubin Report.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.612
- Thanks for having me.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.180
- All right.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.315
So we crunched some numbers
before we had you on today.

00:00:49.315 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've got the papers right
in front of me here.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.953
Now we just gave
Ukraine 40 billion.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.356
According to my numbers,
we don't have 40 billion.

00:00:56.356 --> 00:00:57.424
Am I correct?

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.627 line:0%
- No, even before we
started, you know,

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:04.664 line:0%
lavishing large sums
on the COVID bailout,

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:06.733
we were already about
a trillion dollar short

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.435
in our ordinary expenses.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
So to pay for
Medicare, Medicaid,

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:14.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
food stamps, social
security, and the military

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.976
we're about a trillion
dollars short every year.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.211
Now in the last two years,

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:20.080
we added an extra
4 or 5 trillion

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.616
just to really show people we
could spend money like crazy

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.186 align:start size:97% position:3%
but our normal expenses were
a trillion dollars short.

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:27.954
And so that's the
question I asked,

00:01:27.954 --> 00:01:29.823
where does the 40
billion come from?

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:30.757
Who do you get it from?

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.225
Do you get it from,

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:35.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
do we borrow it from China
to send it to Ukraine?

00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:36.896
Really, we borrow it from China,

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:39.165
we borrow it from England,
we borrow it from Japan,

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.067
but a lot of it we print.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.469
And all the Republicans up here

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.637 align:start size:84% position:16%
seem to be concerned
about inflation

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.106 align:start size:84% position:16%
but they don't seem
to be concerned

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
about where they're
gonna find the 40 billion

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.375
they sent to Ukraine.

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:52.745
- Are you shocked
how few Republicans

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.314 align:start size:81% position:19%
decided to push
back against this?

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:57.784 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think what, it was 14
total, if I'm not mistaken.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:01:59.486
- Yeah, it was a small
number in the Senate.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.088
So, you know, it's about
20% of the Republicans,

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:04.057
about 10% of the Senate.

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:07.026 align:start size:97% position:3%
And over in the house, there
are about 57 Republicans.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.596 align:start size:97% position:3%
But frankly, I look at the
list and I say, you know what?

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm not really
gonna be supporting

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
or working for any people
who say that they are

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.202 align:start size:84% position:16%
for a constitutional
foreign policy

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
and yet are for shoveling
money out the door.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.073 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, we do have
problems at home.

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:22.442 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm worried about us
becoming Venezuela, frankly.

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:24.944 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm worried about us
destroying our currency.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.113
And I see no,

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:29.482
everybody that looks at this
even the people who look at it

00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:32.118 align:start size:97% position:3%
from the traditional central
banking point of view,

00:02:32.118 --> 00:02:33.686
say we're so far
behind the curve.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.555
They're not sure how
this is gonna end.

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.790
Because when interest
rates are still so low

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:39.125
and they've been so slow

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:41.995
to start increasing
the interest rates,

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.229
many people are predicting

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.298
there isn't going to be
a quick end inflation

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:46.900
that could get much worse.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.201
What if we have 15

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:51.871
or 20% inflation by by
November or December?

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:55.074 align:start position:0%
We're talking about an alarming
problem where, you know,

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.709
the poor and working
class in our country

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.679
won't be able to afford the
routine staples of life.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.014
But we're then talking also

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.883 align:start size:88% position:13%
about what happens
when it finally bursts.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.385
And when it bursts

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:08.154
usually you have dramatic
rises in interest rates

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:11.191 align:start size:97% position:3%
but you also have dramatically
high unemployment.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:13.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm concerned about
the future of our country.

00:03:13.793 --> 00:03:16.596
And I think we need to
get our house in order.

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.031
- All right.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:19.566 align:start size:97% position:3%
We're not very good at
getting our house in order.

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.301
We seem to wanna get other
people's houses in order.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:22.902 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we don't do that
very well either.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.137
This 40 billion though,

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:25.405
one of the things
that you brought up

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:27.640
in the last week or so was,

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
hey guys, how about we
get some receipts on this?

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:32.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
How about we find out
exactly where it's going,

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.513
what you're gonna
be spending in on,

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:97% position:3%
who's getting the kickbacks,
et cetera, et cetera.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:39.319
And pretty much nobody
has an answer for you.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.253
Is that fair to say?

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.955
Or is that an overstatement?

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.489
- Well, there's something called

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.659
the special inspector general
of Afghanistan reconstruction.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:48.628
He's been doing this
for several years now.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:52.165
He has a whole team involved,
but Afghanistan, as you know

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:55.568 align:start size:88% position:13%
we decided the best
way to exit was to exit

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.870
in infamy and screw
the whole thing up,

00:03:57.870 --> 00:04:00.573
but leave about 80 billion
worth of equipment there.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:04.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this guy's an amazing,
he has an amazing team

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:06.646 align:start size:84% position:16%
at looking at the
waste and he at least

00:04:06.646 --> 00:04:08.414
stops some of the criminality.

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:10.416 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I do mean
direct criminality.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.785 align:start size:88% position:13%
There are thieves, there
are worldwide thieves

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.089
who suck up US tax payer
dollars and then they run.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.590
One quick example.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:19.726
They built a $90 million hotel,

00:04:19.726 --> 00:04:22.428
or they got $90 million
for a hotel in Kabul.

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:25.665 align:start size:97% position:3%
They spent probably 10
million erected an edifice,

00:04:25.665 --> 00:04:27.300
the basic outline of it.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.801
And then the guy
took off somewhere

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.903 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the middle east and
took the rest of the money.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.405
It still sits there.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.807
It's just an empty edifice,
it didn't quite get built.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.476
And so this kind of
stuff goes on and on.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:38.578
And I thought this
guy would be perfect.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:41.547
His name's John Sopko,
he's done a great job

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:44.617
at looking at Afghan waste
and catching the criminals.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:47.253
Well, everybody came up to
me at first and they said,

00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:49.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
oh it's a great idea,
Republicans and Democrats.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.125
But then they got wind of
who it was going to be.

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:54.527 line:0%
And so the Uber Hawks in
the Republican party said,

00:04:54.527 --> 00:04:55.928 line:0%
oh we hate him

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.998 align:start position:0% line:0%
because he's always embarrassing
us with all our follies.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:00.199
As we go around the world

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.101
he finds where the
money's being stolen.

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:04.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
He's an embarrassment
to the Hawks.

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:05.471
And actually guess what?

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.006
There are Hawks in both parties.

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:10.310 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they both ganged up and
said, oh, no we can't do this.

00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.712
We need to let Biden
pick his own person

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:14.380 align:start size:84% position:16%
which would be
starting from scratch

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:17.083
and would take six months to
a year, might never happen.

00:05:17.083 --> 00:05:19.619
And they would probably
pick someone who's weak,

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:21.387
and will not do the job.

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:24.424 align:start position:0%
So it was a fight, but it shows
how much concern they have.

00:05:24.424 --> 00:05:26.392 align:start size:84% position:16%
They do not have
concern for the money.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:28.795
These people are not
fiscally conservative.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:31.397
And really they wound up
just calling me names,

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:32.899
calling me an isolationist.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:35.168
And it's like, well, no,
I'm a fiscal conservative

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:38.204 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they're not
fiscally conservative.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:40.907 align:start size:97% position:3%
- No, I mean, you were
literally asking for receipts.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:41.941
That's pretty much it.

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:43.476
In a more broad sense,

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.411
in terms of what's
going on in Ukraine,

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:48.481 align:start size:84% position:16%
I know we are
technically not at war

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:51.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we often now go to
wars without declaring war

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.552
and all of that,

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:54.354
and I know your stance
on that and I'm with you,

00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:56.489
but are we at war at this point?

00:05:56.489 --> 00:06:00.026
At what point when you
endlessly fund a war

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:02.128
are you actually at war?

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.630
- I think you're at war

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:07.567
when your enemy perceives
you at war and attacks you.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:10.103
So there's a possibility
and we don't know this.

00:06:10.103 --> 00:06:11.371
If everything goes well,

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.905
and the Ukrainians
keep fighting well

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:14.941
and they push the Russians
out and then the war ends

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:17.810
everybody will have said
it was all worthwhile.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:21.414
But it's just like Finland
and Sweden joining NATO,

00:06:21.414 --> 00:06:23.783
might be a good thing
if nobody attacks 'em

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:26.719
and that's defensive, but it
also might be a bad thing.

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:29.422
What if we decide that we're
going to locate nuclear weapons

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.524
in Finland for 50, 60 years,

00:06:31.524 --> 00:06:33.826 align:start size:97% position:3%
they've said they don't
want nuclear weapons there.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:35.528
You know, what if that's
part of being in NATO.

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:37.530
Part of being in NATO
is sort of accepting

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:39.665
the weapons that
US sends to you.

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.502
So I think we don't know
what if the provocation

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:44.570
does lead to a nuclear exchange.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:47.173 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, if a European
capital is bombed

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:50.109
or a US capital, or
large city is bombed

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:51.611
with nuclear weapons,

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
will people then look back
in retrospect and say,

00:06:53.579 --> 00:06:56.082
well maybe we shouldn't
have pushed them so hard.

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:57.850
Maybe we shouldn't have insisted

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:01.120
that Ukraine be part of NATO.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.989
And, you know, there
are many smart minds

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:04.457
who have written about this.

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:05.758
George Kennan is probably
one of the most famous

00:07:05.758 --> 00:07:07.326
diplomats of the last century

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:10.630 align:start size:97% position:3%
said it was a mistake to
advance and to provoke Russia

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:13.199
with creating NATO
larger and larger.

00:07:13.199 --> 00:07:15.368 align:start size:84% position:16%
So did Kissinger,
so have many others.

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:20.373
So did James Matlock,
who was the ambassador

00:07:21.474 --> 00:07:22.909 align:start size:84% position:16%
under the first
George Bush to Russia.

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.777 align:start size:88% position:13%
So a lot of smart
people written on this,

00:07:24.777 --> 00:07:26.212
but now if you say
anything, they say,

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:28.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
oh you're sympathizing
with Putin.

00:07:28.848 --> 00:07:30.783
Even when I try to
preface every talk

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:33.586
by saying there's
no justification
for Putin's attack.

00:07:33.586 --> 00:07:36.322
There's no sympathy
for Putin at all.

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:38.257 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that I hope
the Ukrainians win,

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:40.693
but it still doesn't
mean we should ignore

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:42.862
the fundamental causes of war

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:45.598 align:start size:84% position:16%
and try to at
least revisit this.

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:48.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we know how to prevent
war in the future.

00:07:48.134 --> 00:07:50.503
I mean, even in the end
of the Ukrainians win,

00:07:50.503 --> 00:07:52.438 align:start size:81% position:19%
there will be a
destroyed country.

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.207
Ukraine will be destroyed,

00:07:54.207 --> 00:07:56.209
and then who's gonna
pay to rebuild Ukraine.

00:07:56.209 --> 00:07:58.411 align:start size:88% position:13%
They're already talking
about us paying.

00:07:58.411 --> 00:08:01.247 align:start position:0%
The 40 billion that we are
spending on the war effort now,

00:08:01.247 --> 00:08:03.616
they're saying that'll
last till September.

00:08:03.616 --> 00:08:06.352 align:start position:0%
They're gonna be back in
September asking for more money.

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:09.455
But the bill when we
go to rebuild Ukraine.

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:10.890
Russia destroys it

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're going to
laugh all the way as we go

00:08:12.692 --> 00:08:15.528
and spend a couple hundred
billion rebuilding Ukraine.

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:18.264 align:start size:84% position:16%
So yeah, we just
don't have the money.

00:08:18.264 --> 00:08:19.632
We're outta money

00:08:19.632 --> 00:08:21.868 align:start size:97% position:3%
for all the stuff we
promised the American people.

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:24.937
- Are you surprised that
some of your colleagues,

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:28.207
guys that I'm sure you
like, and that are smart

00:08:28.207 --> 00:08:29.475
and decent human beings,

00:08:29.475 --> 00:08:32.311
that they just don't get
the basic obvious stuff

00:08:32.311 --> 00:08:33.846
that you just laid out there,

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:36.015
that they don't get once you
start throwing money at it,

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:37.450
you're gonna throw
more money at it

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.951
and it's gonna keep going,

00:08:38.951 --> 00:08:41.487
and we've done this before
and we're gonna do it again?

00:08:42.655 --> 00:08:44.590 align:start size:84% position:16%
- There's a disconnect
between the people.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:45.858
And there's a disconnect

00:08:45.858 --> 00:08:47.727
in particular between
the Republican primary

00:08:47.727 --> 00:08:50.229
and the Republican party
voters and who they get.

00:08:50.229 --> 00:08:52.632
They get a lot of people
who promise 'em many things

00:08:52.632 --> 00:08:54.333
and then don't follow through.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:56.702
Republicans at home and
the Rotary Club will say,

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:58.504
I'm fiscally conservative.

00:08:58.504 --> 00:09:00.806 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they come up here and they
vote for all the spending.

00:09:00.806 --> 00:09:03.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
They go to the Rotary Club
and says, I'm with you,

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:05.678 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you elect me, we will
get rid of Obamacare.

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:08.180
Seven Republicans in
the Senate came back

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.849
and voted to keep Obamacare.

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:11.317
We had the identical vote

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:14.186
under president Obama
when he vetoed it.

00:09:14.186 --> 00:09:16.055 align:start size:84% position:16%
And every Republican
voted for it.

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:17.356
President Trump came in power

00:09:17.356 --> 00:09:19.158
and said he would sign the law.

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:21.527 align:start size:84% position:16%
I introduced the
exact same legislation

00:09:21.527 --> 00:09:23.563 align:start size:81% position:19%
as almost word
for word the same,

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:26.599
and seven Republicans who voted
to get rid of it under Obama

00:09:26.599 --> 00:09:28.200
voted to keep foot under Trump

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:29.969 align:start size:88% position:13%
when we could have
gotten rid of Obamacare.

00:09:29.969 --> 00:09:30.937
This is a problem.

00:09:30.937 --> 00:09:32.672
It's a perpetual problem,

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:35.975
but that hawkishness, some
people define conservatism

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:38.177
as hawkishness, not
fiscal conservatism,

00:09:38.177 --> 00:09:39.712
not balanced budgets.

00:09:39.712 --> 00:09:41.781 align:start size:84% position:16%
They are conservative
only in the sense

00:09:41.781 --> 00:09:44.717
that they are for
a bigger military,

00:09:44.717 --> 00:09:48.554
and more might and that
we should spread freedom

00:09:48.554 --> 00:09:49.755
around the world.

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:51.891 align:start size:88% position:13%
And these are the George
W. Bush Republicans.

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:53.593
And frankly, it's
one of the reasons

00:09:53.593 --> 00:09:57.096
why I lean more towards
Trump on so much of this

00:09:57.096 --> 00:09:58.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that he did have a good
head on his shoulders.

00:09:58.898 --> 00:10:00.299
And he had a certain reticence

00:10:00.299 --> 00:10:01.767
to get involved
around the world.

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:04.937 align:start size:97% position:3%
He wasn't afraid, he was
strong, but at the same time

00:10:04.937 --> 00:10:08.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
he wasn't eager for the
beginnings of a world war.

00:10:08.874 --> 00:10:10.743 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I think in some
ways he was like Reagan.

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:13.379 align:start size:97% position:3%
He actually thought, he
worried about a nuclear war

00:10:13.379 --> 00:10:16.682
and did not want to be
the person who presided

00:10:16.682 --> 00:10:19.218
over the destruction of the
world through nuclear war.

00:10:19.218 --> 00:10:23.422
So he was not eager
to sort of, you know,

00:10:23.422 --> 00:10:25.524
I think provoke war
around the world.

00:10:25.524 --> 00:10:27.493
- I think I mentioned this
to you last time you were on

00:10:27.493 --> 00:10:30.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
but your support for Trump
was one of the things

00:10:30.796 --> 00:10:33.165 align:start size:97% position:3%
that finally got me to
support him because I thought,

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:36.068
all right, here's one of
the guys on the shortlist

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:37.837 align:start size:84% position:16%
of people I respect
in the Senate.

00:10:37.837 --> 00:10:40.039
And he's, you know,
one of Trump's main
defenders right now.

00:10:40.039 --> 00:10:42.575
So let's move to some
other stuff real quick.

00:10:42.575 --> 00:10:46.045 align:start size:97% position:3%
This Ministry of Truth, that
seems to have collapsed.

00:10:46.045 --> 00:10:48.447 align:start size:84% position:16%
You had a rather
extraordinary exchange

00:10:48.447 --> 00:10:50.850
with HHS Secretary Mayorkas.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.885 align:start size:81% position:19%
So I wanna play
just a little bit.

00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:54.253 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Do you think
the Steele dossier

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:57.023
included Russian disinformation?

00:10:57.023 --> 00:11:00.059
- Senator, that's not a question

00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:01.661
that I'm equipped to answer-

00:11:01.661 --> 00:11:02.928
- It was in the public news.

00:11:02.928 --> 00:11:03.863
It was a, you may
have heard of it,

00:11:03.863 --> 00:11:05.197
the Mueller investigation,

00:11:05.197 --> 00:11:07.066 align:start size:84% position:16%
it was a $32 million
investigation

00:11:07.066 --> 00:11:09.502
that went over a
couple of years.

00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:11.170 align:start size:84% position:16%
Horowitz was an
investigator general,

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:13.072
and he looked at
the FBI's activity

00:11:13.072 --> 00:11:14.540
in the beginning of this.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:17.576 align:start size:97% position:3%
And what the FBI concluded
was that there were FBI agents

00:11:17.576 --> 00:11:20.413
throughout this period
of time who concluded

00:11:20.413 --> 00:11:23.816 align:start size:97% position:3%
that yes, the dossier was full
of Russian disinformation.

00:11:23.816 --> 00:11:26.152 align:start size:88% position:13%
So let's say it is,
Russian disinformation.

00:11:26.152 --> 00:11:28.821 align:start position:0%
You say your new
disinformation governance board

00:11:28.821 --> 00:11:31.757 align:start size:97% position:3%
is going to help the
public with disinformation.

00:11:31.757 --> 00:11:33.693 align:start size:88% position:13%
You claim it's not
gonna be about domestic.

00:11:33.693 --> 00:11:36.662 align:start size:97% position:3%
It's gonna be about foreigners
and those evil Russians.

00:11:36.662 --> 00:11:38.197
So here's my question.

00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:40.332 align:start size:84% position:16%
The FBI concludes
that the steel dossier

00:11:40.332 --> 00:11:42.702 align:start size:84% position:16%
was full of Russian
disinformation,

00:11:42.702 --> 00:11:46.872
CNN propagated this
disinformation gladly

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:48.741
for years and years.

00:11:48.741 --> 00:11:50.876 align:start size:88% position:13%
The difference, I guess,
between your opinion

00:11:50.876 --> 00:11:53.879
and our opinion is that
as despicable as it is

00:11:53.879 --> 00:11:56.716
that CNN propagated
this disinformation,

00:11:56.716 --> 00:11:59.351
I wouldn't shut 'em down,
I wouldn't lecture 'em,

00:11:59.351 --> 00:12:00.786
I wouldn't put it on
a government website

00:12:00.786 --> 00:12:04.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
that CNN's wrong for
propagating disinformation.

00:12:04.423 --> 00:12:06.592 align:start size:97% position:3%
The problem you have is
you're not willing to admit,

00:12:06.592 --> 00:12:07.993 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, we can't even
have an agreement

00:12:07.993 --> 00:12:10.296
on what the FBI said
was disinformation.

00:12:10.296 --> 00:12:12.698 align:start size:97% position:3%
How do you propose that
you're going to have an office

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:16.402 align:start size:97% position:3%
of disinformation governance
if you see the problem

00:12:16.402 --> 00:12:18.604 align:start size:88% position:13%
in even determining
what is disinformation?

00:12:18.604 --> 00:12:23.609
- Oh, Senator, because
our work is not focused

00:12:24.477 --> 00:12:27.012
on disinformation with large.

00:12:27.012 --> 00:12:29.315 align:start size:88% position:13%
Where we, the Department
of Homeland Security

00:12:29.315 --> 00:12:33.486
become involved is when
there's a connectivity

00:12:33.486 --> 00:12:37.022 align:start size:84% position:16%
between disinformation
and threats

00:12:37.022 --> 00:12:38.357
to the security of the Homeland.

00:12:38.357 --> 00:12:39.592 align:start size:84% position:16%
Let me-
- Well, that's what

00:12:39.592 --> 00:12:40.793
the Russians might
be considered that.

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:42.194 align:start size:84% position:16%
You mentioned the
Russians the other day

00:12:42.194 --> 00:12:43.429
when you tried to pivot away

00:12:43.429 --> 00:12:45.197
from this being
about censorship.

00:12:45.197 --> 00:12:48.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you've got no idea
what disinformation is

00:12:48.067 --> 00:12:49.802 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I don't think the
government's capable of it.

00:12:49.802 --> 00:12:52.271
Do you know who the greatest
propagator of disinformation

00:12:52.271 --> 00:12:53.773
in the history of the world is?

00:12:53.773 --> 00:12:55.274
The US government.

00:12:55.274 --> 00:12:57.176
Are you familiar with McNamara?

00:12:57.176 --> 00:12:59.278
The Pentagon papers?

00:12:59.278 --> 00:13:01.080
Are you familiar
with George W. Bush

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.082
and the weapons of
mass destruction?

00:13:03.082 --> 00:13:05.885
Are you familiar
with Iran-Contra?

00:13:05.885 --> 00:13:08.287 align:start size:88% position:13%
I mean, think of all
the debates and disputes

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:11.857
we've had over the last
50 years in our country.

00:13:11.857 --> 00:13:13.993
We work them out
by debating them.

00:13:13.993 --> 00:13:15.227
We don't work them out

00:13:15.227 --> 00:13:16.295 align:start size:84% position:16%
by the government
being the arbitrary.

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:18.063
I don't want your guardrails.

00:13:18.063 --> 00:13:20.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want you to have
nothing to do with speech.

00:13:20.232 --> 00:13:22.902
You think we can't
determine, you know,

00:13:22.902 --> 00:13:25.671
speech by traffickers
as disinformation.

00:13:25.671 --> 00:13:27.306
You think the American
people are so stupid

00:13:27.306 --> 00:13:29.441
they need you to tell
them what the truth is.

00:13:29.441 --> 00:13:31.177 align:start size:84% position:16%
You can't even admit
what the truth is

00:13:31.177 --> 00:13:32.678
with the Steel dossier.

00:13:32.678 --> 00:13:35.314
I don't trust government to
figure out what the truth is.

00:13:35.314 --> 00:13:39.118 align:start size:97% position:3%
Government is largely
disseminating disinformation.

00:13:39.118 --> 00:13:41.153
- So when I was playing that
before the show for my guys

00:13:41.153 --> 00:13:43.823 align:start size:97% position:3%
we were all cracking up
because it's like this guy,

00:13:43.823 --> 00:13:47.059
I mean, you cannot even agree
on what disinformation is.

00:13:47.059 --> 00:13:48.694
That was your whole point there.

00:13:48.694 --> 00:13:50.396
That none of this
makes any sense.

00:13:50.396 --> 00:13:53.032
Beyond that, it's against the
First Amendment, let's say

00:13:54.433 --> 00:13:56.602 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, the First Amendment
and constitutionality

00:13:56.602 --> 00:13:58.337 align:start size:88% position:13%
doesn't work with
these people very well.

00:13:58.337 --> 00:14:00.773 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I tried to get
him at least to admit

00:14:00.773 --> 00:14:02.842
that he really didn't even agree

00:14:02.842 --> 00:14:05.578
with the FBI on what
disinformation was.

00:14:05.578 --> 00:14:07.780 align:start size:84% position:16%
We had the Christopher
Steele dossier.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:11.550
The FBI now admits that it
was Russian disinformation.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.652
In fact, Christopher Steel's
said he got the information

00:14:13.652 --> 00:14:15.120
from a source in the Kremlin.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.122 align:start size:84% position:16%
Yeah, I think it might
have been a source

00:14:17.122 --> 00:14:19.091
giving him disinformation.

00:14:19.091 --> 00:14:20.426
So anyway, I ask him about it.

00:14:20.426 --> 00:14:21.961
I love the deflection.

00:14:21.961 --> 00:14:24.563
He's like, well, you know,
I'm not an expert in that.

00:14:24.563 --> 00:14:27.266 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I say, well, do
you read the newspaper?

00:14:28.701 --> 00:14:31.537
We spent $30 million on it
and we spent countless hours

00:14:31.537 --> 00:14:33.205
on television talking about it.

00:14:33.205 --> 00:14:35.074
And everybody on your side said,

00:14:35.074 --> 00:14:37.676 align:start size:88% position:13%
it was Russian collusion
that Trump colluded.

00:14:37.676 --> 00:14:39.778
But it turns out that
was disinformation.

00:14:39.778 --> 00:14:42.681 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I said, if
that's disinformation

00:14:42.681 --> 00:14:45.384 align:start size:84% position:16%
are you gonna go to
CNN and shut down CNN?

00:14:45.384 --> 00:14:46.552
Because for the last three years

00:14:46.552 --> 00:14:48.520 align:start size:84% position:16%
they've been promoting
disinformation.

00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:50.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, for the
record, I'm not for that.

00:14:50.756 --> 00:14:52.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Right.
- I say, turn the channel.

00:14:52.892 --> 00:14:54.226
If you don't like CNN.

00:14:54.226 --> 00:14:57.363 align:start position:0%
And they're full of
disinformation, which they are,

00:14:57.363 --> 00:15:00.733
turn the channel, but
I'm afraid of any kind

00:15:00.733 --> 00:15:03.669 align:start size:97% position:3%
of government organization,
even one that would go

00:15:03.669 --> 00:15:05.271
after the disinformation of CNN.

00:15:05.271 --> 00:15:06.572
I don't want the
government anywhere

00:15:06.572 --> 00:15:08.340
near determining what truth is.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.709
It's not as easy as
a job as you think.

00:15:10.709 --> 00:15:12.244
You hear facts on both sides.

00:15:12.244 --> 00:15:16.081
It's like being a juror or a
journalist or even a scientist.

00:15:16.081 --> 00:15:17.783
You hear a lot of the
facts on each side,

00:15:17.783 --> 00:15:19.585
and then you try to
draw a conclusion,

00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:22.021
but it's not always easy
and definable in something

00:15:22.021 --> 00:15:24.523
that somebody from government
could be trusted with that job

00:15:24.523 --> 00:15:26.025 align:start size:84% position:16%
- In all your years
in the Senate,

00:15:26.025 --> 00:15:28.694 align:start size:97% position:3%
have you ever seen anything
that was more a direct assault

00:15:28.694 --> 00:15:30.129
on the First Amendment

00:15:30.129 --> 00:15:32.498 align:start size:97% position:3%
than the idea of this
proposed Ministry of Truth?

00:15:32.498 --> 00:15:35.701 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, the idea that
the government would
somehow regulate

00:15:35.701 --> 00:15:39.571 align:start size:84% position:16%
or punish or depress
certain speech?

00:15:40.773 --> 00:15:42.274
- I'm worried about it,
'cause there are people

00:15:42.274 --> 00:15:44.376
on the left and the right
sort of promoting this.

00:15:44.376 --> 00:15:46.645
And I tell my audiences
all the time now back

00:15:46.645 --> 00:15:48.514 align:start size:88% position:13%
at home because they're
really proud of me

00:15:48.514 --> 00:15:50.316 align:start size:81% position:19%
on fighting the
Ministry of Truth.

00:15:50.316 --> 00:15:52.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I said, look,
there's some on the right

00:15:52.318 --> 00:15:53.752
who are setting up legislation

00:15:53.752 --> 00:15:55.621 align:start size:84% position:16%
where there would
be government boards

00:15:55.621 --> 00:15:57.289
because they hate
big tech so much

00:15:57.289 --> 00:16:00.159 align:start size:84% position:16%
that they want
oversight of big tech.

00:16:00.159 --> 00:16:02.962 align:start position:0% line:0%
And so we have to be very
worried about right or the left

00:16:02.962 --> 00:16:06.198
getting involved with speech
and people need to remember

00:16:06.198 --> 00:16:08.567
there are tons and
tons of choices.

00:16:08.567 --> 00:16:11.704
Your podcast didn't
exist 20 years ago.

00:16:11.704 --> 00:16:14.573 align:start size:97% position:3%
You know, when I was a
kid, you had three networks

00:16:14.573 --> 00:16:16.108 align:start size:84% position:16%
you didn't really have
conservative radio.

00:16:16.108 --> 00:16:18.243
You had ABC NBC and CBS.

00:16:18.243 --> 00:16:19.778
The news was identical

00:16:19.778 --> 00:16:21.680 align:start size:88% position:13%
and it was a very
subtle form of leftism.

00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:24.116
It wasn't in your face,
but it was all liberal

00:16:24.116 --> 00:16:25.684
but there were no other choices.

00:16:25.684 --> 00:16:28.287
We've got all kinds of
choices on television now

00:16:28.287 --> 00:16:29.288
on the right,.

00:16:29.288 --> 00:16:30.990
We have conservative radio.

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:33.092
We dominate the radio sphere.

00:16:33.092 --> 00:16:34.960
We have the podcast sphere.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.796
So I don't worry about us
getting enough message out.

00:16:37.796 --> 00:16:39.665
And I tell people
I'm kind of tired

00:16:39.665 --> 00:16:42.167 align:start size:88% position:13%
of everybody that
complains about Twitter,

00:16:42.167 --> 00:16:44.303
quit using it, go
somewhere else.

00:16:44.303 --> 00:16:45.704
You know, I left YouTube.

00:16:45.704 --> 00:16:47.139
I haven't yet left Twitter

00:16:47.139 --> 00:16:49.575
but I left YouTube
and came to Rumble

00:16:49.575 --> 00:16:52.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
because I don't
wanna support a group

00:16:52.311 --> 00:16:53.612
that believes in censorship.

00:16:53.612 --> 00:16:55.514 align:start size:84% position:16%
And if the others
continue to censor me,

00:16:55.514 --> 00:16:57.216
I'll leave them too.

00:16:57.216 --> 00:16:58.417
- Let me ask you
one other thing.

00:16:58.417 --> 00:17:00.019 align:start size:84% position:16%
'Cause I know you're
limited on time.

00:17:00.019 --> 00:17:01.854 align:start size:88% position:13%
I've come to the
conclusion at this point

00:17:01.854 --> 00:17:04.790 align:start size:88% position:13%
that this administration
cannot be this inept

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:08.894
that all of the problems with
supply chain and inflation

00:17:08.894 --> 00:17:13.065 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the bungling of Ukraine
and all of the stuff

00:17:13.065 --> 00:17:14.967
this cannot be ineptitude.

00:17:14.967 --> 00:17:16.902
This has to be intentional.

00:17:16.902 --> 00:17:18.637
Am I being,

00:17:18.637 --> 00:17:20.773
am I overstepping do
you think on that?

00:17:22.408 --> 00:17:23.842 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Only if their
party is a death wish

00:17:23.842 --> 00:17:25.944
'cause I think they're
gonna get steamrolled

00:17:25.944 --> 00:17:28.180
in November because
of the inflation.

00:17:28.180 --> 00:17:29.648
No, I think they

00:17:29.648 --> 00:17:31.984
they really don't really
truly understand inflation.

00:17:31.984 --> 00:17:33.585
Maybe they're dumb
enough to believe

00:17:33.585 --> 00:17:35.587
that greed causes inflation,

00:17:35.587 --> 00:17:37.289
but inflation comes from debt

00:17:37.289 --> 00:17:39.191 align:start size:97% position:3%
and it comes from the federal
reserve buying the debt

00:17:39.191 --> 00:17:40.526
and all that new demand,

00:17:40.526 --> 00:17:42.361
all that new money that
flows into the system

00:17:42.361 --> 00:17:43.829
bids prices up.

00:17:43.829 --> 00:17:45.264 align:start size:81% position:19%
With gasoline,
they made it worse

00:17:45.264 --> 00:17:47.633
by also restricting the supply.

00:17:47.633 --> 00:17:50.235
So prices, supply and demand.

00:17:50.235 --> 00:17:52.805
You reduce the supply,
increase the demand.

00:17:52.805 --> 00:17:55.240
And boy, do you have
rip-roaring inflation?

00:17:55.240 --> 00:17:58.277
But we've borrowed more money
in the last two years ever

00:17:58.277 --> 00:17:59.878
even as a percentage of GDP

00:17:59.878 --> 00:18:02.181 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you try to
quantify it that way,

00:18:02.181 --> 00:18:04.216 align:start size:81% position:19%
more money than
we ever had before

00:18:04.216 --> 00:18:06.018 align:start size:84% position:16%
and you even have
Democrat economists,

00:18:06.018 --> 00:18:07.820
there was the firm and came out

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:10.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the last couple of days
on of Obama's economist

00:18:10.489 --> 00:18:12.091
saying it was a mistake.

00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:13.826
They juiced up the
economy too much.

00:18:13.826 --> 00:18:15.794 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he said, I warned
him at the time.

00:18:15.794 --> 00:18:17.863 align:start size:84% position:16%
So there are some
reasonable, rational

00:18:17.863 --> 00:18:20.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
democratic economists,
maybe one or two.

00:18:20.666 --> 00:18:22.568
But anyway, there's a
